Standalone correctness test for ViterbiDecoderIS136
===================================================

Checks the decoder against all four shipped datasets (zeros, ones, gett,
toggle) without building the full EEMBC test harness. For each dataset it
compares every decoded word to the golden output, prints the th_lite CRC16
(so a pass here implies a pass under the harness NON_INTRUSIVE_CRC_CHECK),
and shows the decoded text. Exit code is 0 if all pass, 1 otherwise.

Run (from the viterb00/ directory):

    make -C test check

or from this directory:

    make check

Files:
    selftest.c    the test driver (includes ../viterb00.c and ../datasets/*)
    makefile      builds selftest against ../viterb00.c
    stub/thlib.h  minimal type typedefs so the harness is not needed

Notes:
  - Only gcc/cc is required; no harness, no platform AL layer.
  - This tests correctness, not performance. Timing/throughput still comes
    from the normal EEMBC build (make in the telecom/ directory).
  - If you change the branch metric in viterb00.c (e.g. to Hamming distance),
    the gett and toggle goldens will no longer match unless you regenerate
    them; zeros and ones pass under any sane metric.
